{0 Ocsigen tutorial}

Ocsigen is a framework for client/server Web and mobile applications in
OCaml. This tutorial shows how to use it, from a first application to
advanced features. If you do not know where to begin, read the
{{!page-intro}introduction}.

To install Ocsigen, follow the
{{:https://ocsigen.org/install}installation instructions}. The opam package
[ocsigen] installs the main libraries this tutorial uses.

The reference manuals and APIs of these libraries are in their own
packages: {{!/eliom/page-index}Eliom},
{{!/ocsigenserver/page-index}Ocsigen Server},
{{!/ocsigen-start/page-index}Ocsigen Start},
{{!/ocsigen-toolkit/page-index}Ocsigen Toolkit},
{{!/js_of_ocaml/page-index}Js_of_ocaml}, {{!/tyxml/page-index}TyXML} and
{{!/lwt/page-index}Lwt}.

